WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.434
-Welcome to the show. Welcome back to the show.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:05.534
And I do want to say a sincere thank you so much.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.100
'Cause during the pandemic,

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.734
we were doing the show from my home,

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:12.801
and you were nice enough to do a whole video

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:15.534
and performance for us, and I really appreciate that.

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:16.868
I'll never forget it.

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:18.133
-My wife directed that. -Yeah.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.067
-And I think my children were shouting in the ba--

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.701
We were all figuring out what it was like.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.634
-We didn't know what it was, but you set the tone,

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:25.267
and I appreciate you being there when we needed you.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:27.200
Thank you. I won't forget that. -You're looking very grown-up.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.000
-Yeah. Am I? Yeah. [ Laughter ]

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
I'm still not, though. I'm still not.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.234
-It's a good start. -I appreciate it, yeah.

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:36.434
I want to talk to you about "Self-Titled."

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:40.067
But I also want to talk to you about "Ted Lasso."

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:43.667
Because you do the theme and all the music for "Ted Lasso."

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.734
-Yeah. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.934
Yeah.

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:50.434
I spent like six months of my life...

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:52.734
-Yeah. -...doing that first season.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.267
And I scored the whole thing,

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.133
which is a nightmare, complete nightmare.

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:58.267
-Especially during -- It was during the pandemic?

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.834
-It was awful, yeah, and I had to learn how

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.567
all the buttons in my studio work because my --

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:03.200
Obviously I wasn't allowed to have an engineer

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.901
in the same room and stuff. -Of course.

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:06.534
-And it was just a complete nightmare.

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:07.701
Uploading files, not my jam.

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:10.501
-No. -And all that anyone

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:12.501
really knows about it is like...

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.033
[Imitates song intro] ♪ Yeah ♪

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.434
And then "skip intro."

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:18.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.501
And they're not really -- That's it.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.734
-That's very funny.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:26.467
So you can perform that at your show if you want to.

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:27.767
-Yeah, yeah. I do every night. I just...

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.501
[Imitates song intro] ♪ Yea-- ♪

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:31.267
-There you go. Right. That's it. Then leave.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.601
"Good night, everybody!" -Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:33.667
-The shortest concert.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:34.801
-They got their money's worth, yeah.

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:37.167
-How did you get involved with that?

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.934
-I met Jason Sudeikis upstairs doing "SNL."

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:42.033
-Is that right? -Yeah, first time we did "SNL,"

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:44.467
we met and we did a Beatles sketch together.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:45.801
It was very fun. -Yeah.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:48.300
-And then we stayed in touch, and then I knew about

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.601
his little bits as Lasso that he did as ads early on.

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:54.834
And I'm a big soccer fan, as you would say. Football.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:57.234
-Yeah. Soccer. -Football.

00:01:57.234 --> 00:01:59.300
-Soccer. -No, it's football.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.901
And then he told me he was doing the show, and I loved it.

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:04.667
And then he left me like 400 hours' worth of voice memos.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.200
He loves -- He loves the voice memos.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.267
-He really loves the voice memos. That's how we talk.

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:10.501
-Gotta wade through all them. -That's how he communicates.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:13.133
-It's a nightmare. Yeah. -Yeah.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.601
I wanted to ask you about this

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.667
because I think this is a very cool opportunity.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.868
But you were invited to the Vatican...

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:20.400
-I was, yeah. -...to meet the Pope.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.767
-To meet the -- Papa. -Yeah.

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.934
-Yeah. -I mean, that's a big deal.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.534
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.400
-Is it -- Is there rules you have to follow?

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.367
Is it nerve-racking? Is it...?

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.701
-Yeah, it was -- No, it wasn't nerve-racking.

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:34.133
I'd had zero responsibilities, so I was up for it.

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:35.300
-Yeah.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.567
-I didn't have to do anything or say anything.

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.133
I just wanted to kind of hear him.

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:41.200
You know? He's got a tough gig. -Yeah, he does. I'd say.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.567
-And, you know, I think as popes go, I --

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:44.901
He seems like a good one.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:46.601
But the bar is pretty low, you know?

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.701
-Yeah, no, he's -- -Just historically speaking,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:49.801
the bar's pretty -- -Yes.

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:51.200
-He's nice -- He's a nice fellow.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.000
-He's a good pope, yeah, as far as Popes go.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.634
And you didn't say much? -I didn't say much, no.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:58.567
But I did -- You know, you have your, like,

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.234
private moment with him at the end.

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:02.100
And I was in line.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.434
And I get that he's sitting down,

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.968
and so I knelt down.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:09.067
I think he thought I was taking a knee, which I wasn't.

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:10.601
But he was like, "No, stand up."

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:12.033
And then I had to sort of crouch over.

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.801
It was really uncomfortable. Anyway, and then he --

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:15.901
The only thing he said to me was like, "Will you pray for me?"

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:19.567
And where I'm from, you know, I'm like, "Yeah, love to, yes."

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:22.434
Slap an arm on his shoulder and say a quick prayer for him.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:26.767
And what I didn't realize was my friend was filming it.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.701
And I'm praying -- I've got my eyes closed.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.334
It lasts about eight seconds.

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.767
And as he's sat there, holding my hand, and my arm's like --

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.734
And he just does a little cheeky check of the watch.

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.200
-The Pope?! -Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.601
Just a quick -- And then, "Thank you very much."

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:43.734
-No.

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:46.534
-It was great. It was great. It was lovely.

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.968
-Oh, my gosh. -Yeah. He was very sweet.

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:51.000
-You actually brought us the video from that moment.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.767
[ Audience cheering ] -Let's show the video.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.501
-I've not seen it. I've not seen it yet.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.033
-Have you not seen it yet? -No, no.

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:57.567
Please. Let's -- Let's take a look.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:58.934
-Yeah, I'll do -- I'll do the commentary.

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.601
I'll do the highlight reel. Ready?

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.200
There we go. "Oh, will you pray for me?"

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.667
"Yeah, sure, mate. Yeah, Lord bless him.

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:05.634
You know, he's got a tough gig."

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.801
And then he's just, "Ah, thanks so much."

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:10.067
Just quickly -- Just -- Just gonna...

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:11.701
just gonna check the time.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:14.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:18.067
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:20.634
Ah. I'm so happy.

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.300
[ Applause ]

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.567
-You can't write that. -It wasn't that long.

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.334
-You can't write that. -It wasn't that long.

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:28.467
It's not like I was praying in tongues or something.

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.834
-It wasn't that long at all. He's like, "I think we --

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:33.133
I think we've kind of had enough here. Yeah, yeah, okay."

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:34.801
-"Yeah, just -- That's probably enough."

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.067
-That is classic.

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:37.667
-Bless him. He meets so many people.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.167
-That is classic. -Must be rough.

00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:41.367
-Oh, my gosh. No, please. Thank you for bringing that.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:42.901
-That is unbelievable.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:45.067
Marcus, let's talk about "Self-Titled."

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.767
Why did you call it "Self-Titled"?

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:48.000
Why didn't you call it "Marcus Mumford"?

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.267
-Just too much of my name.

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:51.734
-Too much -- -You know what I mean?

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:53.334
-"Marcus Mumford, Marcus Mumford." It's just too much.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:54.767
-Too much. -Too much.

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:57.000
And I like the idea that other people

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.167
could kind of insert their own selves into it

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:02.534
and see some of their own story in it or whatever.

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:04.467
-Do you -- Is that the way you write your songs?

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:06.200
-No, but I think that's the magic of songs.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.801
Like, you write them, you know,

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:09.567
in these personal, private moments,

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:11.567
and then the weirdest thing in the world,

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.367
you make them as public as possible.

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:15.167
Which is just strange. -Yeah, yeah.

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:16.968
-But there's some magic that happens

00:05:16.968 --> 00:05:19.167
when people can sort of relate their own story

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:22.133
to whatever story you've written in your songs, and I like that.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:24.934
-Yeah. The video for "Cannibal,"

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:28.133
by the way, was directed by --

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:29.934
-A little-known, up-and-coming.

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:32.067
-Yeah, up-and-coming director Steven Spielberg.

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:33.434
-Yeah.

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:36.100
I've always believed in fostering new talent.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.701
-You are always -- -You know.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:39.767
-You're always there helping out the new people.

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.033
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:42.501
He's never done one before, so I was like --

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:44.400
-Yeah, he's never done one? -He's never done a music video.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.300
-How did you get him involved with this?

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:50.167
-He and Kate Capshaw, his wife, were some of the first people

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:52.734
outside of my little circle to hear the record.

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:55.367
And Kate -- They sent me a video of them dancing

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.167
in their kitchen, which I didn't bring...

00:05:57.167 --> 00:05:59.534
-Yeah. -...to one of the songs.

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:03.300
And so it was just last-minute basically

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.601
and, um, just did it on a phone. -Yeah.

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:08.934
But you did bring us a photo of -- of what Steven Spielberg

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:11.200
directing looks like.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.067
And this is -- this is fantastic.

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:16.501
Just look at it.

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:18.801
He's in a rolling chair...

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:21.334
on an iPhone, and that's Kate, right?

00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:22.734
-That does kind of sum it up.

00:06:22.734 --> 00:06:24.334
Kate's the one doing all the work, right?

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:27.868
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. -He takes all the glory.

00:06:27.868 --> 00:06:30.434
But it was this amazing teamwork thing,

00:06:30.434 --> 00:06:33.634
where there's this zoom-in, so we used a wheelie chair.

00:06:33.634 --> 00:06:36.734
I mean, this was the extent of the production.

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:39.400
-I mean, was he like -- Was he cool with it?

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.167
-I think my wife got -- my wife credited with "wardrobe."

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:44.033
Easiest gig she's ever had. -Did she really?

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:45.033
-I'm wearing black.

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:46.334
-You're just wearing a tee, yeah.

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:48.033
-And then -- And Kate did all the work.

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:49.901
And then -- And he just did it on his phone.

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:51.334
-And what's he like directing you?

00:06:51.334 --> 00:06:52.901
Did -- Did you ask him for direction?

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:55.901
-Yeah, I did. I told him to tell me exactly what to do

00:06:55.901 --> 00:06:57.667
and I'd just play the song.

00:06:57.667 --> 00:07:00.200
And he started -- Actually, the first time we did it,

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.534
he shot, like -- I was playing guitar like this.

00:07:02.534 --> 00:07:04.901
And he's here with his phone looking up.

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:06.167
And I was just insecure

00:07:06.167 --> 00:07:07.968
about the number of chins I had that day.

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:10.934
But I was basically like, "Maybe we can start from above?"

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:12.834
And -- And so he tried it.

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:15.234
And then as we're looking back at it on his phone, he's like,

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:18.267
"Oh, that's cool. It's like "Indy 3."

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:20.400
Which is an "Indiana Jones" reference.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.100
-What?! -And Steven Spielberg --

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.868
And it's the bit, you know, at the beginning

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:25.868
when Harrison Ford has his head down with the hat,

00:07:25.868 --> 00:07:27.767
then he looks up and gets smacked in the face. I was like --

00:07:27.767 --> 00:07:29.534
-You can't make an "Indiana Jones" --

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:31.133
-Spielberg just made that reference.

00:07:31.133 --> 00:07:32.167
-Yes! -To me!

00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:36.300
-You won! You won. You won the year.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.334
-Have you been -- You were in --

00:07:38.334 --> 00:07:41.267
I noticed this when I really re-watched "Band of Brothers."

00:07:41.267 --> 00:07:42.400
-Oh, yeah.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.701
-You were in one of those episodes.

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:45.367
-Oh, well, thank you. Hold your applause.

00:07:45.367 --> 00:07:47.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:48.667
-You are. You drive a Jeep. -Yes, I --

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:50.667
-I have not been prepped for this. This is not --

00:07:50.667 --> 00:07:52.834
I recognized your face. -Yeah.

00:07:52.834 --> 00:07:55.367
Did I take you out of the experience?

00:07:55.367 --> 00:07:56.834
-No, you didn't. I -- I remember --

00:07:56.834 --> 00:07:58.801
The first time I watched it was before I knew who you were.

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:00.200
-Yeah. And you said --

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.100
-And the second time I watched it, a vague recollection.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.801
-You go, "That's guy's got something."

00:08:03.801 --> 00:08:06.267
-And it's in the Battle of the -- one of the Battle --

00:08:06.267 --> 00:08:07.767
one of the two Battle of the Bulge episodes.

00:08:07.767 --> 00:08:08.901
-Yeah. And I didn't --

00:08:08.901 --> 00:08:10.000
-But he didn't direct that one, right?

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:11.968
-No. He was -- -It's alright, mate.

00:08:11.968 --> 00:08:14.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:17.467 --> 00:08:19.033
Don't worry. It's nice to have goals.

00:08:19.033 --> 00:08:21.467
-Yeah, it's cool. You know, even when you see this photo,

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:24.033
you can see him almost checking his watch as he's doing it.

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:25.567
[ Laughter ]

00:08:25.567 --> 00:08:30.067
Marcus Mumford. "Self-Titled" is available now.

00:08:30.067 --> 00:08:34.100
Marcus is performing for us with Monica Martin after the break.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.133
Stick around, everybody. Come on back.

